WEBVTT

00:00:01.453 --> 00:00:04.994
It seems today
 that all you see

00:00:04.996 --> 00:00:08.181
Is violence in movies
 and sex on TV

00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:11.517
But where are those
 good old-fashioned values

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:14.687
On which we used to rely?

00:00:14.764 --> 00:00:18.283
Lucky there's a family guy

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.629
Lucky there's a man who
 positively can do

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.154
All the things that make us

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:24.891
Laugh and cry

00:00:24.916 --> 00:00:30.046
He's... a...
 Fam... ily... Guy!

00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:35.875
We now return to Jack Ryan,

00:00:35.877 --> 00:00:38.712
starring the guy who used
 to smirk a lot on The Office.

00:00:40.048 --> 00:00:42.382
Jack, we launched the drone
strike against the terrorists

00:00:42.384 --> 00:00:44.910
like you suggested,
but hit a hospital instead.

00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:47.979
What are you doing?
Six people died.

00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:51.435
Oh, I get it.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.069
The joke is his hair
isn't fully combed.

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:56.306
Wait, what happened?

00:00:56.532 --> 00:00:58.865
Oh, your mom bought an app
that cuts power to the TV

00:00:58.867 --> 00:01:01.310
once I've reached
my daily screen time limit.

00:01:01.386 --> 00:01:02.477
Peter, the app
says that--

00:01:02.554 --> 00:01:04.538
-I know!
-Keep it down, guys.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.723
I'm trying to land
a 757 in Dubai

00:01:06.748 --> 00:01:08.765
with a crosswind
and a broken landing gear.

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:10.819
For the last week,
Brian's been getting into

00:01:10.876 --> 00:01:12.940
some stupid flight simulator
game.

00:01:13.081 --> 00:01:15.673
It's not stupid.
And I'm fairly amazing at it.

00:01:15.751 --> 00:01:17.267
Earlier, I landed in Texas,

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.510
not gonna tell you the city
'cause it affects the joke,

00:01:19.588 --> 00:01:20.937
but when I landed, I said,

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.450
"Houston, we don't
have a problem."

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:25.696
What? What was the city?

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:31.781
And another perfect landing.
Check it out.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.950
Oh, I can't even look at screens
over shoulders.

00:01:34.124 --> 00:01:36.186
- Lois said.
- Peter, the app just--

00:01:36.211 --> 00:01:37.197
I'm not looking!

00:01:40.803 --> 00:01:43.701
All right, time to finally
organize this closet.

00:01:43.779 --> 00:01:45.628
Let's see what we got. Uh...

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.056
Packaging from every
Apple product we own

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:50.633
'cause it seems too nice
to just throw away.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.619
Oh, look it's Mommy's
old Easy-Bake Oven

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:55.788
from when she was a girl.

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:57.774
If it's not big enough for you
to stick your head in,

00:01:57.776 --> 00:01:58.958
I have no interest.

00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:01.334
Stewie, you might like
playing with this.

00:02:01.359 --> 00:02:03.100
Ooh, I'll go get a rag
to clean it.

00:02:03.106 --> 00:02:06.215
Don't bother. I don't need
your stupid garbage girl toys

00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:07.942
from the 1940s, grandma!

00:02:07.967 --> 00:02:09.391
I love trucks and dinosaurs--

00:02:09.521 --> 00:02:12.130
Oh, my God, Rupert, I've always
wanted an Easy-Bake Oven!

00:02:12.207 --> 00:02:13.798
Oh, I haven't been this excited
since we watched

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.800
the series finale of Caillou.

00:02:32.265 --> 00:02:35.403
Don't stop believin'

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.574
Hold on to that feelin'

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.218
Street lights, people

00:02:48.143 --> 00:02:49.459
Don't stop--

00:02:57.065 --> 00:02:58.818
Huh. Looks like
Jerome's switching

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.595
to all recycled paper goods.

00:03:00.672 --> 00:03:03.172
Joe, don't punish us just
'cause you forgot your phone.

00:03:03.197 --> 00:03:05.575
I didn't forget it. I asked
Bonnie why she looked so tired

00:03:05.627 --> 00:03:06.960
and she hucked it in the pool.

00:03:06.962 --> 00:03:08.385
Whew, pretty windy out there.

00:03:08.432 --> 00:03:10.646
Feels like 21 knots coming in
from the southwest.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:11.573
Right, Quagmire?

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:12.982
What-- What is this?

00:03:13.275 --> 00:03:15.410
Ah, nothing, I'm just talking
a little shop with you

00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:18.008
now that I've officially
entered your world.

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:19.489
"Entered my world"?

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:20.823
Yeah, I've been
totally crushing it

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.234
on this flight simulator app,
and now I realize

00:03:23.311 --> 00:03:26.312
flying a plane is nowhere
near as hard as I thought.

00:03:26.314 --> 00:03:29.165
Brian, don't belittle
the expertise my job requires.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.335
Playing a game on an iPad
and flying a commercial airliner

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:33.928
are two very different things.

00:03:34.105 --> 00:03:36.105
Whoa, running into
a bit of headwind here.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.774
Brian, there is no way you
could ever do what I do.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.017
Has anybody ever made a joke

00:03:40.095 --> 00:03:41.870
about the quality
of paper straws?

00:03:41.905 --> 00:03:45.331
Because I just thought
of a pretty hot take.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.441
Stewie, what is that
incredible smell?

00:03:55.677 --> 00:03:57.868
Just a simple pizza I thought
Rupert might like.

00:03:57.946 --> 00:03:59.536
You know, since he's
a basic little bitch

00:03:59.614 --> 00:04:00.930
who shops at Filene's.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.733
Well, it's delicious.

00:04:03.735 --> 00:04:05.751
Almost as good as Caserta's.

00:04:05.828 --> 00:04:07.753
Thanks, but Caserta's
is no Arturo's.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.847
Ever had Arturo's?

00:04:08.923 --> 00:04:11.757
No, but nothing
can top DiPetrillo's.

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:13.926
Mr. DiPetrillo is from Sicily

00:04:13.928 --> 00:04:16.913
and makes all the dough
by hand every morning.

00:04:16.992 --> 00:04:18.433
Did I tell you I met him?

00:04:18.545 --> 00:04:21.036
No, no, I would've remembered
because I wouldn't have cared.

00:04:21.262 --> 00:04:23.736
Stewie, this is amazing pizza.

00:04:23.761 --> 00:04:26.583
You know, I feel like maybe
you and I could open up

00:04:26.608 --> 00:04:29.108
a really successful
boutique pizza place.

00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:30.760
Are you serious? I'm in.

00:04:30.762 --> 00:04:32.853
But mostly to get
a Michelin star.

00:04:32.931 --> 00:04:35.615
It's always been my dream
to have my culinary talents

00:04:35.617 --> 00:04:38.167
validated in print
by a tire company.

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:45.315
Okay, and final thing
before we push back,

00:04:45.376 --> 00:04:48.013
which six seats do you want
to disable the TVs on?

00:04:48.103 --> 00:04:50.347
-Morning, boys.
-Brian? What are you doing?

00:04:50.372 --> 00:04:52.448
Only qualified personnel
are allowed in here.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.225
Then why do all pilots
leave the door open

00:04:54.302 --> 00:04:55.393
when people are boarding?

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.620
We-- We're supposed
to help hand out

00:04:57.622 --> 00:04:59.564
mileage plan credit card
applications.

00:04:59.682 --> 00:05:01.958
But why are you even here?
You're going to Orlando?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.460
Yeah. I took what you said
the other night to heart

00:05:04.462 --> 00:05:06.796
and I've enrolled in a flight
training school in Florida

00:05:06.798 --> 00:05:08.406
called Huffman Aviation.

00:05:08.483 --> 00:05:11.225
Isn't... Isn't that where
the 9/11 hijackers trained?

00:05:11.302 --> 00:05:12.726
I don't know,
I just used a coupon.

00:05:12.804 --> 00:05:13.894
Just take your seat.

00:05:14.897 --> 00:05:15.855
I-I mean,

00:05:15.912 --> 00:05:18.917
would you like to earn 10,000
bonus miles by applying today

00:05:18.993 --> 00:05:21.711
for the Transnational Airlines
Mastercard?

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.831
Hey there, how are you doing?

00:05:25.908 --> 00:05:27.516
Just so you know,
as of this year,

00:05:27.518 --> 00:05:29.485
I'm allowed to hit you
as hard as I can.

00:05:29.487 --> 00:05:30.762
Out of my way!

00:05:33.324 --> 00:05:34.837
Jim, are you okay?

00:05:34.918 --> 00:05:36.199
I think he's got food poisoning.

00:05:36.224 --> 00:05:38.494
It must've been that
sack lunch of leftover shrimp

00:05:38.513 --> 00:05:39.753
from his niece's wedding.

00:05:39.831 --> 00:05:41.439
Well, thank God
you didn't have any.

00:05:41.516 --> 00:05:43.424
Well, actually, he kept waving
the bag in my face and asking,

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:45.851
"Does this taste funny to you?"
I-I didn't want to be rude.

00:05:47.763 --> 00:05:49.263
Ah! It's coming!

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.949
Don't worry, Quagmire,
I can take over.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.509
Are you crazy? You could
never in a million yea--

00:05:53.511 --> 00:05:54.953
Ah! Son of a bitch!

00:05:55.029 --> 00:05:56.454
Dammit! Get out of the way!

00:05:56.531 --> 00:05:57.956
I'm gonna have
to take a boy band.

00:05:58.168 --> 00:06:00.152
-What does that mean?
-"In sink."

00:06:00.228 --> 00:06:02.351
I also would've accepted
"back-streak boys."

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:05.204
And it's definitely coming out
at "98 degrees"

00:06:05.437 --> 00:06:07.023
in "one direction."

00:06:07.122 --> 00:06:09.662
In any case, it's all gonna
sound and smell terrible.

00:06:10.346 --> 00:06:11.243
I'm taking over.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.153
No, Brian, don't you
touch anything!

00:06:13.178 --> 00:06:14.344
Look, I got this.

00:06:14.399 --> 00:06:17.550
Ladies and gentlemen,
prepare for landing.

00:06:21.906 --> 00:06:23.906
Hey, my TV stopped working.

00:06:23.908 --> 00:06:25.391
And now mine's working.

00:06:33.418 --> 00:06:35.251
Lower your flaps more and...

00:06:35.253 --> 00:06:37.486
-...ease off the throttle.
-Roger that.

00:06:57.866 --> 00:07:00.255
I don't believe it.
He actually pulled it off.

00:07:00.703 --> 00:07:02.828
Welcome to Orlando.
And as a reminder,

00:07:02.905 --> 00:07:05.464
there are a few passengers
who have a very short turnaround

00:07:05.541 --> 00:07:07.892
to meet their drug dealers,
 so if you could clear the aise

00:07:07.969 --> 00:07:09.618
and let them off first,
 that'd be great.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:10.803
-Excuse me.
-Pardon me.

00:07:10.976 --> 00:07:12.327
-Thank you.
-Thank you, guys.

00:07:18.245 --> 00:07:20.396
Today, we honor
two brave citizens

00:07:20.398 --> 00:07:22.414
who showed coolness
under pressure

00:07:22.491 --> 00:07:25.158
to get that plane
safely on the ground.

00:07:25.186 --> 00:07:27.295
Now, if someone could hold
these giant scissors...

00:07:27.371 --> 00:07:29.297
I needed them for
the thing before this,

00:07:29.373 --> 00:07:32.115
and the thing after this,
but not for this.

00:07:32.709 --> 00:07:36.712
Brian, Glenn, please accept
these keys to the city.

00:07:36.864 --> 00:07:38.197
A lot about being mayor

00:07:38.199 --> 00:07:40.975
is having enormous
junk drawer things.

00:07:43.047 --> 00:07:45.063
Gentlemen, Tom Tucker,
Channel 5 News.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.039
Quite an honor
for you two today.

00:07:47.041 --> 00:07:48.164
Is there a question in there?

00:07:48.189 --> 00:07:50.709
Honestly, Tom, I was just
grateful to be on scene

00:07:50.711 --> 00:07:52.044
-and able to help.
-Terrific.

00:07:52.046 --> 00:07:53.896
So, two-part question
for both of you:

00:07:53.972 --> 00:07:55.806
Brian, does the weather
outside today

00:07:55.883 --> 00:07:57.399
-seem "comfortable"?
-No.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:07:59.476
And, Glenn, if you were
a producer and you said

00:07:59.554 --> 00:08:01.737
to your talent that it was
"comfortable" outside--

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:04.314
Could've brought a coat, Tom.
I'm not your mother.

00:08:04.339 --> 00:08:05.838
Well, that'll do it
from City Hall.

00:08:05.893 --> 00:08:08.227
This is Tom Tucker
reporting live on the scene

00:08:08.229 --> 00:08:10.245
because it's close
to my son's karate thing.

00:08:10.544 --> 00:08:13.490
Hi, you two. I'm Keith, the
lowest-level executive possible

00:08:13.568 --> 00:08:14.900
from Transnational Airlines.

00:08:14.902 --> 00:08:17.069
Listen, you two are
great on camera together,

00:08:17.071 --> 00:08:19.760
and people love this
feel-good story of heroism.

00:08:19.975 --> 00:08:22.516
We'd like to send you both
on a multi-state press tour

00:08:22.541 --> 00:08:24.191
to share your story.

00:08:24.245 --> 00:08:25.761
Really? That'd be amazing.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.188
Eh, I don't know...

00:08:27.264 --> 00:08:29.765
It'll be great PR.
You saved a ton of lives.

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.100
You're actually friends.

00:08:31.176 --> 00:08:32.843
And we could use
something like this

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:35.104
after that toilet flush
sucked in a baby.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.864
Yeah, I'm not sure
a press tour is--

00:08:36.941 --> 00:08:38.924
And I forgot to mention
that, as a pilot,

00:08:38.926 --> 00:08:40.926
you are contractually obligated

00:08:40.928 --> 00:08:42.778
to represent the airline
to the media.

00:08:43.837 --> 00:08:44.597
Come on, Quagmire,

00:08:44.599 --> 00:08:46.782
we might actually have fun
together on a press tour.

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:48.283
I mean, crazier things
have happened.

00:08:48.443 --> 00:08:50.024
Look at Pete Davidson's
love life.

00:08:50.337 --> 00:08:51.660
I just text them back promptly.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.547
That's it. That's the secret.

00:09:01.616 --> 00:09:03.966
Stewie, the line is huge.

00:09:03.968 --> 00:09:06.877
How did we get so many customers
right out of the gate?

00:09:06.904 --> 00:09:09.738
Oh, I-I see,
you're calling us a pop-up.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:12.257
Oh, yeah, you do that and
white people go frickin' crazy.

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:15.002
-I saw this place on Facebook.
-I saw it on TikTok.

00:09:15.079 --> 00:09:16.670
I read a blurb
in Parade magazine.

00:09:16.747 --> 00:09:19.915
Did you know LeAnn Rimes is
happier than she's ever been?

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:20.892
Can I get a slice?

00:09:20.958 --> 00:09:22.509
Okay, let's start
with the easy one:

00:09:22.567 --> 00:09:23.990
we don't do "slices."

00:09:24.088 --> 00:09:26.255
Next, you can start
by scanning the QR code

00:09:26.257 --> 00:09:27.871
to enter yourself in the raffle.

00:09:28.442 --> 00:09:30.534
Ooh, is that an Android? Here.

00:09:30.611 --> 00:09:32.033
What's this, your website?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.656
No, it's the number
for Domino's.

00:09:33.734 --> 00:09:34.628
Take a hike, idiot.

00:09:34.783 --> 00:09:37.959
Domino's. We meet
the legal definition of "pizza."

00:09:42.201 --> 00:09:43.021
Pharmacy.

00:09:44.168 --> 00:09:45.685
Refill a prescription.

00:09:46.702 --> 00:09:48.260
Refill a prescription.

00:09:49.463 --> 00:09:50.930
Representative.

00:09:51.874 --> 00:09:53.616
Speak to a representative.

00:09:53.618 --> 00:09:54.783
Will you quit
doing personal crap

00:09:54.785 --> 00:09:56.261
and focus on our interview?

00:09:56.514 --> 00:09:57.286
Okay, we're almost ready,

00:09:57.288 --> 00:09:59.212
but just so we get
the on-screen labels correct,

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.789
you're the one
who landed the plane,

00:10:00.791 --> 00:10:02.808
and you're the one
who pooped in the sink?

00:10:06.705 --> 00:10:08.614
Welcome back
to Good Morning, Akron,

00:10:08.639 --> 00:10:10.966
Ohio's only
opioid-free morning show.

00:10:11.218 --> 00:10:15.061
Brian, Glenn, how do you prepare
for an emergency like this?

00:10:15.139 --> 00:10:16.747
Well, all pilots
are highly trained--

00:10:16.824 --> 00:10:18.645
There's no training
for a moment like this.

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:20.993
You're just relying
on pure gut instinct.

00:10:21.195 --> 00:10:23.103
But when you've landed at
as many airports as I have--

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.104
On an iPad.

00:10:24.181 --> 00:10:25.289
--you draw on that experience--

00:10:25.366 --> 00:10:27.124
It's an app that costs $2.99.

00:10:27.201 --> 00:10:29.034
--to the point where it's
almost like muscle memory.

00:10:29.111 --> 00:10:30.461
You can also get
the app for free,

00:10:30.537 --> 00:10:32.704
but you have to sit through
a lot of ads for the Army.

00:10:33.137 --> 00:10:35.700
These guys are good.
We gotta get this on the road.

00:10:35.725 --> 00:10:37.833
-Wheels up, Jack.
-It's Jacqueline now.

00:10:38.045 --> 00:10:40.696
And back to HR I go.

00:10:40.909 --> 00:10:42.455
You know, when you take off,
you never think

00:10:42.533 --> 00:10:44.457
you're gonna see your pilot
pooping in the sink.

00:10:44.535 --> 00:10:47.311
But a real hero knows
that's when you have to step up.

00:10:47.388 --> 00:10:49.462
Well, it's a good question,
but I think I knew

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.464
within a couple minutes
of taking the first bite.

00:10:51.466 --> 00:10:53.709
You only end up using
like three of those buttons.

00:10:53.711 --> 00:10:55.560
I thought those guys
were, like, geniuses.

00:10:55.637 --> 00:10:58.155
Well, I've read that shrimp is
actually supposed to be cooked

00:10:58.232 --> 00:10:59.973
to 140 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:11:04.896 --> 00:11:07.406
I-I can't do
the noises, but y-you get it.

00:11:08.893 --> 00:11:10.167
Diarrhea, diarrhea, diarrhea.

00:11:10.244 --> 00:11:12.461
I can't do the noises,
but you get it.

00:11:16.289 --> 00:11:17.490
Stewie, check it out.

00:11:17.568 --> 00:11:19.492
Dave Portnoy
from Barstool Sports

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.920
just tweeted he's coming
to our restaurant tomorrow

00:11:21.997 --> 00:11:24.848
to do one of his
One Bite Pizza Reviews.

00:11:24.925 --> 00:11:26.591
Awesome. Who's Dave Portnoy?

00:11:26.768 --> 00:11:30.012
He's like if a high-school
athlete got one genie wish.

00:11:30.014 --> 00:11:32.681
But he also happens to be
one of the most influential

00:11:32.683 --> 00:11:35.183
pizza place kingmakers
on the internet.

00:11:35.185 --> 00:11:36.868
Really? Chris, that's fantastic.

00:11:37.041 --> 00:11:38.186
I know.

00:11:38.188 --> 00:11:40.297
And we better get started now,

00:11:40.299 --> 00:11:43.425
'cause he likes
his pizza extra crispy.

00:11:44.983 --> 00:11:46.583
Uh, wh-- what was that?

00:11:47.932 --> 00:11:49.355
Oh, this is not good.

00:11:49.433 --> 00:11:51.450
The light bulb in
the Easy-Bake Oven burned out.

00:11:51.813 --> 00:11:54.527
That's fine, we have tons of
light bulbs in the house.

00:11:54.605 --> 00:11:55.546
Chris, we're in trouble.

00:11:55.622 --> 00:11:58.123
This is a custom bulb
from the 1960s.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.199
It's 200 watts

00:11:59.218 --> 00:12:00.943
and made with 40% lead.

00:12:00.945 --> 00:12:02.052
There's literally nobody

00:12:02.129 --> 00:12:04.054
who would have
a light bulb this old.

00:12:05.783 --> 00:12:07.641
There might be one person.

00:12:12.506 --> 00:12:14.732
Oh, there you are, Jesse.

00:12:19.777 --> 00:12:22.130
Man, Arnie is
so excited for you guys

00:12:22.132 --> 00:12:23.465
to do this ad for him.

00:12:23.467 --> 00:12:24.724
So, what, now we're pitchmen?

00:12:24.802 --> 00:12:27.970
Guys, this is free advertising
for the airline,

00:12:27.972 --> 00:12:29.562
and we could
use the distraction.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:32.732
We, uh... we dragged another
Asian doctor off a plane.

00:12:32.927 --> 00:12:34.227
Okay, let's roll it.

00:12:34.772 --> 00:12:36.979
Hi, I'm local hero
Brian Griffin.

00:12:37.228 --> 00:12:39.590
And I'm
Glenn "Diarrhea" Quagmire.

00:12:39.615 --> 00:12:40.856
If you're looking to buy a car,

00:12:40.985 --> 00:12:42.667
you want to make
a smooth landing,

00:12:42.744 --> 00:12:44.410
not take a dump in the sink.

00:12:44.488 --> 00:12:45.596
That's right. So, come on down

00:12:45.672 --> 00:12:48.991
to Brockner Toyota
for some explosive deals.

00:12:49.143 --> 00:12:50.751
If you're hunting for a car,

00:12:50.827 --> 00:12:52.494
don't pull a "Quagmire."

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:54.570
Sorry, sorry,
what the hell is this?

00:12:54.625 --> 00:12:57.793
Oh, Mr. Brockner always likes
to have some humor in his ads.

00:12:58.074 --> 00:13:00.335
Humor? Some fat guy
pretending to be me

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:02.245
pooping in a sink is the humor?

00:13:02.458 --> 00:13:03.581
Damn it, Brian, that's enough.

00:13:03.606 --> 00:13:04.939
I was in the military,

00:13:04.964 --> 00:13:07.434
and I have worked
for 25 years in aviation.

00:13:07.511 --> 00:13:09.603
My whole life,
I dreamed that someday,

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.497
maybe I'd even have my own
Sully Sullenberger moment.

00:13:12.499 --> 00:13:13.774
But it'll never happen now.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.234
Have you tried Googling me?
It's just this!

00:13:17.491 --> 00:13:20.505
Yeah. Wow, and if you
Google Image "diarrhea,"

00:13:20.507 --> 00:13:22.340
it's just pictures of
you and George Brett.

00:13:22.359 --> 00:13:24.859
Not only am I not getting
the respect I deserve,

00:13:24.936 --> 00:13:26.769
but I'm the punchline in a story

00:13:26.847 --> 00:13:28.438
where you're the hero. You!

00:13:28.798 --> 00:13:30.365
You know what, I quit.

00:13:30.442 --> 00:13:31.792
Wait, you can't
quit the press tour.

00:13:31.868 --> 00:13:32.875
It's in your contract.

00:13:32.914 --> 00:13:34.519
Plus, we've still got
one more event to do.

00:13:34.521 --> 00:13:36.021
Oh, I'm finishing
the press tour.

00:13:36.023 --> 00:13:38.114
A pilot always lands the plane.

00:13:38.139 --> 00:13:40.080
I meant that
I quit being a pilot.

00:13:40.484 --> 00:13:41.193
Where are you going?

00:13:41.195 --> 00:13:42.613
To be alone and think.

00:13:48.988 --> 00:13:50.268
This is how pilots do it.

00:13:56.196 --> 00:13:59.194
I bought a mattress
 at the wrong store.

00:13:59.196 --> 00:14:00.637
Don't "Quagmire" the bed.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:02.820
Shop the Weekapaug Sleep Outlet.

00:14:03.049 --> 00:14:04.474
This mattress commercial

00:14:04.626 --> 00:14:06.384
feels very similar
to that car commercial.

00:14:10.057 --> 00:14:11.406
What the hell's Quagmire doing?

00:14:11.431 --> 00:14:14.616
It looks like he's throwing away
all his pilot uniforms.

00:14:14.745 --> 00:14:15.605
Yeah, he, uh...

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.320
he said he was quitting his job.

00:14:17.714 --> 00:14:19.339
I think the press tour's
been a little rough on him.

00:14:19.525 --> 00:14:21.134
He's throwing out
the pants, too?

00:14:21.235 --> 00:14:23.326
Those are just blue pants.
Someone could wear those.

00:14:23.403 --> 00:14:25.237
"Rough on him?"
In... in what way?

00:14:25.414 --> 00:14:26.755
I don't know,
like maybe he feels bad

00:14:26.831 --> 00:14:29.090
I stole his thunder
by landing his plane.

00:14:29.267 --> 00:14:30.784
This shirt
with those blue pants?

00:14:30.861 --> 00:14:32.510
Could be a sweet look
for the club.

00:14:32.512 --> 00:14:34.604
Well, I watched
those interviews, Brian.

00:14:34.681 --> 00:14:36.848
You weren't exactly
gracious to him.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.441
Or maybe the night
before a wedding.

00:14:38.518 --> 00:14:40.185
I'm getting those pants.

00:14:40.187 --> 00:14:41.536
Lois, this is not my fault.

00:14:41.847 --> 00:14:43.688
Was I supposed to
not land that plane?

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.690
And, come on, it's not like
Quagmire's a saint.

00:14:45.692 --> 00:14:46.875
You know what he's like.

00:14:46.951 --> 00:14:49.694
Yes, we all know
the bad things about Quagmire,

00:14:49.696 --> 00:14:51.621
but you took away
his one good thing.

00:14:51.698 --> 00:14:54.975
If nothing else, he's always
been an outstanding pilot.

00:14:55.051 --> 00:14:57.460
It's the only thing anyone
ever respected about him.

00:14:57.537 --> 00:14:58.703
Lois is right, Brian.

00:14:58.705 --> 00:15:00.705
Wearing that pilot's hat
means something.

00:15:00.707 --> 00:15:02.575
It's one of
the few remaining hat jobs.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:04.758
You guys are right.

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:06.613
I gotta fix things
with Quagmire.

00:15:07.214 --> 00:15:08.971
In fact,
I'm gonna see him tomorrow

00:15:09.049 --> 00:15:10.306
for our last press appearance,

00:15:10.308 --> 00:15:12.308
and I know just how
to make things better.

00:15:12.592 --> 00:15:14.977
Is the room getting spinny
to anyone else?

00:15:15.055 --> 00:15:16.559
Peter, take those pants off.

00:15:16.584 --> 00:15:18.400
I can't, my arms are numb.

00:15:21.771 --> 00:15:23.289
So, what's the plan? We just ask

00:15:23.314 --> 00:15:25.580
for one of his light
bulbs from the 1960s?

00:15:25.605 --> 00:15:26.506
Oh, no way.

00:15:26.583 --> 00:15:28.249
Mr. Herbert's really weird

00:15:28.274 --> 00:15:29.214
about his possessions.

00:15:29.419 --> 00:15:31.011
He lived through the Depression,

00:15:31.087 --> 00:15:32.888
so he hangs onto everything.

00:15:34.645 --> 00:15:36.886
Oh, well, look who it is.

00:15:37.755 --> 00:15:39.058
Do come in.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:41.095
What brings you boys by?

00:15:41.172 --> 00:15:42.522
Actually, Mr. Herbert,

00:15:42.599 --> 00:15:45.083
I, uh, noticed
a new mole on my thigh

00:15:45.085 --> 00:15:48.102
and wanted to ask
if it looks misshapen to you.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.668
Well, let's have
a little look-see.

00:16:18.677 --> 00:16:21.472
There's not one book in here
that's a real book.

00:16:28.311 --> 00:16:29.364
Ah! Damn it.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:32.513
There it is. What do you think?

00:16:32.707 --> 00:16:34.184
Merciful heavens.

00:16:36.194 --> 00:16:37.177
Ah, got it.

00:16:38.412 --> 00:16:39.020
Do you hear

00:16:39.096 --> 00:16:41.015
those muffled cries
in the next room?

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:41.816
It's the TV.

00:16:41.841 --> 00:16:43.027
Doesn't sound like the--

00:16:43.052 --> 00:16:45.090
We've got pizza to make.
It's the TV.

00:16:51.776 --> 00:16:53.442
Look, I know you're still mad,

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:54.702
but this is our last event,

00:16:54.779 --> 00:16:56.445
so let's make the best of it.

00:16:57.974 --> 00:17:00.491
Oh, my God. Is he okay?

00:17:00.568 --> 00:17:02.143
Say, will you look at that?

00:17:02.145 --> 00:17:04.812
Seems like maybe
it's someone's big chance

00:17:04.814 --> 00:17:06.429
to step up and be the hero.

00:17:06.454 --> 00:17:07.711
What? What's going on?

00:17:07.801 --> 00:17:10.093
I may have unplugged
his insulin pump,

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:13.412
but I'm guessing somebody
knows how to drive this thing.

00:17:13.414 --> 00:17:15.432
Why the hell would I know
how to drive a boat?

00:17:15.508 --> 00:17:16.826
I don't-- I mean,

00:17:16.851 --> 00:17:18.776
isn't it all
kind of the same thing?

00:17:24.668 --> 00:17:27.277
You really "Quagmire'd"
this whole thing, Brian.

00:17:27.302 --> 00:17:29.043
God, now I'm doing it.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.211
Dave Portnoy's gonna be here
any minute to do his review.

00:17:37.364 --> 00:17:38.972
Oh, God, I think that's him.

00:17:40.867 --> 00:17:41.866
Hey, how you doing?

00:17:41.868 --> 00:17:43.051
Dave Portnoy
from Barstool Sports.

00:17:43.127 --> 00:17:45.461
Wow. Welcome, Mr. Portnoy.

00:17:45.539 --> 00:17:46.888
Aw, come on, please.
Call me Dave.

00:17:46.964 --> 00:17:49.316
"Mr. Portnoy" is how I'm
referred to in court documents.

00:17:49.372 --> 00:17:51.298
Well, we are
very excited for you

00:17:51.394 --> 00:17:55.488
to "One Bite Review"
our pizza... Dave.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.856
Whoa, spectacular undercarriage.

00:17:59.881 --> 00:18:01.579
Zero flop. I am hopeful.

00:18:03.309 --> 00:18:04.864
Oh, this pizza's amazing.

00:18:04.941 --> 00:18:06.107
Once I post my review,

00:18:06.183 --> 00:18:07.700
you guys'll have a line
from here to Boston

00:18:07.737 --> 00:18:10.330
filled with nothing but
UFC fans and insurrectionists.

00:18:10.799 --> 00:18:12.354
Did you hear that, Stewie?

00:18:12.379 --> 00:18:13.837
We're gonna be rich.

00:18:14.142 --> 00:18:16.617
Sorry, but the health
department sent me over

00:18:16.694 --> 00:18:18.711
-to ask a few questions.
-Okay.

00:18:18.788 --> 00:18:20.938
-Do you have a business license?
-No.

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:22.940
-Do you have
proper refrigeration?
-No.

00:18:22.942 --> 00:18:24.533
Did either of you
wash your hands

00:18:24.611 --> 00:18:26.534
-before making this pizza?
-No.

00:18:26.559 --> 00:18:28.225
Have either of you
ever washed your hands?

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.105
-No.
-Are either of you

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.462
currently crapping your pants?

00:18:31.709 --> 00:18:33.134
-Yes.
-A little bit, yes.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.453
Okay, listen. I'm not here
to give you a hard time.

00:18:35.455 --> 00:18:36.545
You're a small business.

00:18:36.623 --> 00:18:38.306
I'm willing
to let this stuff slide.

00:18:38.308 --> 00:18:39.974
Oh, uh, there's
one other question here.

00:18:40.051 --> 00:18:42.217
Do you have
a handicap access ramp?

00:18:42.295 --> 00:18:43.461
No.

00:18:43.463 --> 00:18:45.071
You people are animals!

00:18:45.148 --> 00:18:46.739
I'm shutting this place down.

00:18:48.381 --> 00:18:49.884
Well, Chris, we had a good run.

00:18:49.909 --> 00:18:51.316
We sure did.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:53.729
Hey, Meg, where'd
you get those pants?

00:18:53.807 --> 00:18:55.048
They were just on the ground.

00:18:55.177 --> 00:18:56.747
Well, I'm off to the club.

00:19:01.647 --> 00:19:02.905
Come on, stupid boat.

00:19:03.024 --> 00:19:04.777
Okay, I think
if I can just point us

00:19:04.802 --> 00:19:05.984
a bit more that way...

00:19:06.227 --> 00:19:08.486
Oh, crap,
it's the Block Island ferry!

00:19:10.338 --> 00:19:11.143
Aw, snap!

00:19:11.274 --> 00:19:12.990
Don't try to
appear young right now.

00:19:35.882 --> 00:19:37.348
Damn it, Brian,
look what you did!

00:19:37.367 --> 00:19:38.532
What the hell were you thinking?

00:19:38.609 --> 00:19:40.017
I'm so sorry, Quagmire.

00:19:40.276 --> 00:19:41.702
I just saw
how much you'd been hurt

00:19:41.779 --> 00:19:43.199
by all that had happened,

00:19:43.629 --> 00:19:44.856
and I guess
I just wanted to give you

00:19:44.858 --> 00:19:47.024
your Sully Sullenberger moment.

00:19:47.171 --> 00:19:49.337
I clearly screwed that up,
but the truth is

00:19:49.492 --> 00:19:50.992
you're a hero every day

00:19:51.017 --> 00:19:53.381
just by getting people safely
to their destination.

00:19:54.835 --> 00:19:56.701
Wow. Thanks, Brian.

00:19:56.703 --> 00:19:57.810
And, hey, on the bright side,

00:19:57.887 --> 00:19:59.537
you saved all these people
on the duck boat.

00:19:59.539 --> 00:20:01.539
The media will
definitely recognize you

00:20:01.541 --> 00:20:02.527
as a hero now.

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:04.310
A duck boat helmed by

00:20:04.335 --> 00:20:06.744
local diarrhea celebrity
 Glenn Quagmire

00:20:06.746 --> 00:20:08.245
collided with a ferry today,

00:20:08.247 --> 00:20:11.098
blocking the only shipping lane
 into Quahog Harbor.

00:20:11.175 --> 00:20:13.842
The complete blockage will
 result in months-long delays

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.011
in the delivery of goods,

00:20:15.036 --> 00:20:17.353
including shipments of hops
 for beer-making,

00:20:17.378 --> 00:20:19.545
acne medicine,
 and hair dye for men.

00:20:20.995 --> 00:20:22.737
Mmm, this used to be a town

00:20:22.762 --> 00:20:24.161
where a man could keep a secret.

00:20:30.353 --> 00:20:31.444
Well, Brian, thanks to you,

00:20:31.521 --> 00:20:33.446
every store shelf
in town is empty,

00:20:33.548 --> 00:20:35.122
but at least
you landed that plane.

00:20:35.218 --> 00:20:37.235
No one can ever
take that away from you.

00:20:37.439 --> 00:20:40.794
The FAA released data today
 from the black box of a plane

00:20:40.947 --> 00:20:43.130
that recently saw
 an emergency landing

00:20:43.207 --> 00:20:45.116
by civilian passenger
 Brian Griffin.

00:20:45.141 --> 00:20:46.823
According to
 the newly recovered data,

00:20:46.953 --> 00:20:48.786
the airplane's autopilot system

00:20:48.788 --> 00:20:49.970
actually landed the plane

00:20:49.995 --> 00:20:51.686
- and not Brian.
- Ha!

00:20:52.049 --> 00:20:53.065
That's our show for tonight.

00:20:53.142 --> 00:20:55.292
And now,
 the Channel Five theme music

00:20:55.294 --> 00:20:57.886
while our audio guy
 forgets to mute my mic.

00:20:58.981 --> 00:20:59.906
Anyway, as I was saying,

00:20:59.982 --> 00:21:01.574
in exchange for sex,

00:21:01.599 --> 00:21:03.649
I'll help advance your career.